WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.530
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:12.800 --> 00:13.840
Back in the day...

3
00:15.600 --> 00:17.040
I used to play basketball all the time,

4
00:18.280 --> 00:20.280
but once I started working, there was...

5
00:24.480 --> 00:25.920
There was hardly any time left.

6
00:27.120 --> 00:28.360
Do I still have the moves?

7
00:31.080 --> 00:31.880
Yes, you do.

8
00:57.720 --> 00:58.680
Give me a hand here.

9
01:00.280 --> 01:01.280
I'm going to take my pants off.

10
01:31.039 --> 01:32.280
I'll turn the water on for you.

11
01:32.800 --> 01:33.800
Wait.

12
01:40.080 --> 01:40.920
See?

13
01:41.800 --> 01:42.840
I can't even stand up.

14
01:54.080 --> 01:55.280
Help me get into the tub.

15
01:57.240 --> 02:00.520
Also, could you grab me a bathrobe?

16
02:21.200 --> 02:22.280
What are you so shy about?

17
02:22.960 --> 02:24.040
We have the same parts.

18
02:27.920 --> 02:29.400
Could you pull me up?

19
03:03.280 --> 03:04.200
Did you know...

20
03:04.760 --> 03:06.240
building a body like this...

21
03:07.600 --> 03:09.240
takes more than just working out?

22
03:09.560 --> 03:10.240
I didn't.

23
03:11.200 --> 03:12.320
The most important part is...

24
03:13.840 --> 03:15.320
right here.

25
03:19.320 --> 03:21.320
Do you know how important the waist is?

26
03:23.200 --> 03:24.720
You'll understand once you're older.

27
03:28.760 --> 03:30.160
Have you ever slept with anyone?

28
03:32.760 --> 03:33.760
The noodles are ready.

29
03:34.120 --> 03:35.079
I'll go get them.

30
03:55.280 --> 03:56.240
Whoa.

31
03:58.240 --> 04:00.240
This looks good.

32
04:01.240 --> 04:03.120
I didn't know you were such a good cook.

33
04:04.880 --> 04:06.560
I'm only doing this because I hurt your leg.

34
04:06.840 --> 04:08.560
-Want to have some? -No, thanks.

35
04:08.800 --> 04:10.000
Oh, leaving already?

36
04:11.040 --> 04:12.440
I have plans to have dinner with Itt.

37
04:13.960 --> 04:16.360
Hey, don't tell him I sprained my ankle,

38
04:16.399 --> 04:18.399
or he'll rush over here, okay?

39
04:18.800 --> 04:19.360
Yeah.

40
07:24.880 --> 07:25.640
Hey.

41
07:28.440 --> 07:29.680
Isn't that a bit too formal?

42
07:30.880 --> 07:33.200
First impressions are everything.

43
07:33.960 --> 07:35.400
You're dressed way too casually.

44
07:35.840 --> 07:37.920
You're going to get an earful from my brother.

45
07:38.480 --> 07:39.760
Isn't this normal?

46
07:40.240 --> 07:40.960
Why?

47
07:41.640 --> 07:42.960
Worried I won't be around to help you?

48
07:43.800 --> 07:46.240
You promised you'd help me.

49
07:46.280 --> 07:47.720
Yeah, I will. Let's go.

50
08:01.200 --> 08:02.200
Mr. Ing,

51
08:02.720 --> 08:04.880
the document you just signed was...

52
08:04.880 --> 08:07.160
a request to increase the budget

53
08:07.200 --> 08:08.400
by over 20 million.

54
08:09.040 --> 08:09.840
So?

55
08:10.200 --> 08:12.280
Look, Secretary Piang.

56
08:12.800 --> 08:13.920
Don't be such a stress-head.

57
08:15.240 --> 08:17.520
Try to enjoy life, would you?

58
08:18.600 --> 08:20.200
Just look at me.

59
08:20.240 --> 08:21.560
Right now, I'm...

60
08:21.600 --> 08:24.080
enjoying the taste of victory before it's mine

61
08:24.120 --> 08:26.920
because the key to Pattaya...

62
08:27.480 --> 08:29.120
is about to walk right through that door.

63
08:29.680 --> 08:30.880
Oh, Mr. Yok...

64
08:31.560 --> 08:32.120
Exactly.

65
08:32.559 --> 08:33.720
Understood.

66
08:34.159 --> 08:34.960
In that case,

67
08:35.000 --> 08:36.400
I'll arrange a desk for Mr. Yok

68
08:36.400 --> 08:38.159
as close to your office as possible.

69
08:38.159 --> 08:40.559
I'll also set the AC to the perfect temperature

70
08:40.559 --> 08:41.960
and give him the best view.

71
08:42.000 --> 08:45.160
If anyone so much as lays a finger

72
08:45.160 --> 08:46.000
on him,

73
08:46.040 --> 08:47.280
the fire alarm will go off immediately.

74
08:47.560 --> 08:48.360
Secretary Piang,

75
08:48.400 --> 08:48.960
could you check

76
08:48.960 --> 08:50.240
if there are any site visits

77
08:50.280 --> 08:51.440
on our schedule?

78
08:51.480 --> 08:53.680
Do you want to see the site,

79
08:53.720 --> 08:55.520
or do you want to see Mr. Yok?

80
08:58.040 --> 08:59.960
The site, obviously. Why would I want to see Yok?

81
09:00.920 --> 09:02.400
You know, in just...

82
09:03.680 --> 09:06.280
three, two, one...

83
09:21.280 --> 09:23.640
What the fuck?

84
09:24.440 --> 09:27.520
That outfit is a total fashion disaster.

85
09:27.960 --> 09:29.240
What do you think this place is?

86
09:29.400 --> 09:30.520
A playground?

87
09:31.160 --> 09:32.640
If you're here for a stroll, do it outside.

88
09:33.520 --> 09:36.880
I think talent should matter more than an outfit.

89
09:40.120 --> 09:41.000
Secretary Piang,

90
09:41.680 --> 09:43.080
that's Gen Z for you.

91
09:43.360 --> 09:45.360
I like it. It shows character.

92
09:45.880 --> 09:46.680
If you have any questions,

93
09:46.720 --> 09:47.600
ask Piang.

94
09:49.160 --> 09:50.880
Which department should I put them in?

95
09:51.880 --> 09:53.400
Which department do you want to intern at?

96
09:53.760 --> 09:55.760
-I'm fine with anything. -Really?

97
09:55.840 --> 09:56.840
Secretary Piang,

98
09:57.440 --> 09:58.640
have Auntie Chai...

99
09:58.640 --> 09:59.520
transferred to another position,

100
09:59.880 --> 10:02.080
and put Itt in as the housekeeper instead.

101
10:02.120 --> 10:03.560
Fifteen thousand a month, alright?

102
10:04.120 --> 10:04.880
P'Ing,

103
10:04.920 --> 10:06.040
I was just kidding.

104
10:06.040 --> 10:07.160
This is a professional office.

105
10:08.000 --> 10:08.920
What are you supposed to call me?

106
10:10.680 --> 10:11.360
Mr. Ing...

107
10:14.520 --> 10:15.360
Secretary Piang,

108
10:15.400 --> 10:16.520
put Itt

109
10:16.520 --> 10:18.200
in Corporate Development.

110
10:18.200 --> 10:19.520
He'll be right at the front lines

111
10:19.560 --> 10:21.680
so he can finally get some serious work experience.

112
10:21.920 --> 10:24.160
-Mr. Ing... -As for Yok, stay here in this office.

113
10:24.600 --> 10:25.720
You'll be my personal assistant.

114
10:27.640 --> 10:29.920
I know exactly what Itt is capable of.

115
10:30.800 --> 10:32.120
And Yok, you are...

116
10:33.520 --> 10:34.960
a minor in finance

117
10:35.280 --> 10:36.640
with top-tier grades.

118
10:38.000 --> 10:38.960
No wonder

119
10:39.320 --> 10:40.520
you seem so composed.

120
10:40.600 --> 10:42.160
Having you assist me is for the best.

121
10:42.800 --> 10:44.480
Secretary Piang is swamped.

122
10:44.520 --> 10:45.320
You can help her out as well.

123
10:46.160 --> 10:46.880
Understood.

124
10:47.080 --> 10:47.640
Good.

125
10:49.880 --> 10:51.160
Time for some grooming.

126
10:53.400 --> 10:54.360
What do you mean?

127
10:55.600 --> 10:57.040
Having a distinct character is fine,

128
10:57.240 --> 10:58.160
but from now on,

129
10:58.400 --> 10:59.600
you represent me.

130
10:59.880 --> 11:01.240
Come on, let's give you a makeover.

131
11:04.000 --> 11:04.640
I can go buy new clothes

132
11:04.640 --> 11:05.640
with Itt after work.

133
11:05.680 --> 11:06.400
That won't do.

134
11:07.880 --> 11:09.160
My time is too valuable.

135
11:09.160 --> 11:10.400
I can't wait until you're off the clock.

136
11:12.160 --> 11:12.840
What?

137
11:14.880 --> 11:17.200
Do you need a formal letter from the CEO or something?

138
11:17.920 --> 11:18.720
Follow me.

139
11:37.200 --> 11:38.840
Mr. Itt, please follow me

140
11:38.880 --> 11:40.520
to the Corporate Development department.

141
11:40.720 --> 11:42.320
It's the department where...

142
11:45.360 --> 11:46.080
Hey, Pete.

143
11:48.440 --> 11:49.480
Hi.

144
11:49.760 --> 11:51.040
It's been a while, hasn't it?

145
11:52.800 --> 11:55.080
You finally reached out to me.

146
11:55.760 --> 11:57.560
I thought you'd forgotten about your old flame.

147
11:59.520 --> 12:00.680
And...

148
12:02.520 --> 12:03.520
who's this?

149
12:04.560 --> 12:05.280
This is Yok,

150
12:06.000 --> 12:07.240
my new assistant.

151
12:07.560 --> 12:08.520
Oh, my God.

152
12:09.000 --> 12:09.960
He's stunning.

153
12:11.400 --> 12:12.680
His face is a masterpiece.

154
12:14.000 --> 12:15.000
Can I touch him?

155
12:17.280 --> 12:19.400
I'm just going to take some measurements.

156
12:20.920 --> 12:21.960
Measure him carefully.

157
12:22.400 --> 12:24.480
Find a style that I'll actually like.

158
12:26.080 --> 12:26.720
Of course.

159
12:29.720 --> 12:31.400
As for you...

160
12:31.720 --> 12:34.000
-Hurry it up. -Based on, uh...

161
12:35.640 --> 12:36.760
You can try something on.

162
12:36.920 --> 12:38.440
Right this way, please.

163
12:41.200 --> 12:42.160
So handsome.

164
12:43.800 --> 12:44.720
Stunning.

165
12:46.520 --> 12:48.040
Are you ready for the first look?

166
12:48.080 --> 12:48.720
Uh-huh.

167
12:53.880 --> 12:55.440
Ta-da.

168
13:07.960 --> 13:08.600
Okay.

169
13:09.960 --> 13:10.960
Next one.

170
13:16.400 --> 13:18.080
So gorgeous.

171
13:19.040 --> 13:20.280
Wow, so handsome.

172
13:21.960 --> 13:23.920
This one's good. Next.

173
13:26.040 --> 13:27.800
The third look...

174
13:30.880 --> 13:31.920
Next.

175
13:32.600 --> 13:33.280
Are you tired?

176
13:35.920 --> 13:37.480
Ta-da.

177
13:37.520 --> 13:39.160
This is the final look, Ing.

178
13:39.240 --> 13:39.920
Is that it?

179
13:39.960 --> 13:42.360
I actually wanted him to try on ten outfits.

180
13:43.160 --> 13:44.960
Never mind. I'll take them all.

181
13:46.600 --> 13:47.520
I'll be waiting outside.

182
13:47.920 --> 13:48.600
Yes.

183
13:52.200 --> 13:53.640
Here you go.

184
14:02.840 --> 14:03.760
Everything's ready.

185
14:05.840 --> 14:06.680
Thanks a lot.

186
14:07.480 --> 14:09.120
-See you later. -Yeah.

187
14:09.160 --> 14:10.200
See ya.

188
14:12.640 --> 14:14.320
What? Are you not coming?

189
14:15.960 --> 14:18.280
Do you have a thing for the guy with pink hair?

190
14:25.920 --> 14:27.280
Today was exhausting.

191
14:30.040 --> 14:31.440
You're off the clock. Why are you still here?

192
14:32.640 --> 14:33.800
How much did everything cost?

193
14:34.400 --> 14:34.920
What?

194
14:35.800 --> 14:36.960
All these clothes.

195
14:37.880 --> 14:38.680
Oh...

196
14:40.200 --> 14:41.040
I don't know.

197
14:43.320 --> 14:45.080
I'll check the total with P'Piang tomorrow

198
14:45.120 --> 14:46.480
and pay you back right away.

199
14:46.520 --> 14:47.400
Don't worry about it.

200
14:48.200 --> 14:49.200
I bought them for you.

201
14:49.640 --> 14:51.000
Don't worry about the money.

202
14:53.800 --> 14:54.880
Mr. Ing,

203
14:54.920 --> 14:56.800
how could I let you buy all of this for me?

204
14:58.080 --> 15:00.200
Well...

205
15:00.920 --> 15:02.920
I bought these as a gift for you

206
15:03.080 --> 15:04.920
so you'll feel more motivated.

207
15:04.960 --> 15:05.480
Sound good?

208
15:06.280 --> 15:07.920
Thank you, Mr. Ing.

209
15:08.880 --> 15:10.320
But I'd rather just accept

210
15:10.360 --> 15:11.800
your kindness.

211
15:13.520 --> 15:17.200
You truly are Minister Pongpaisan's son.

212
15:17.760 --> 15:20.600
Showing respect to both others and yourself.

213
15:21.000 --> 15:21.720
Okay,

214
15:22.680 --> 15:23.560
you win.

215
15:24.840 --> 15:26.160
I'll put it on my card for now.

216
15:27.120 --> 15:29.960
You can pay me back once you get your salary, okay?

217
15:31.800 --> 15:32.720
Okay.

218
15:32.760 --> 15:35.160
Money isn't the hard part,

219
15:36.400 --> 15:37.680
but the work...

220
15:39.120 --> 15:40.920
is where the real challenge starts.

221
15:41.840 --> 15:43.000
I'm always ready.

222
15:48.080 --> 15:49.400
Excuse me.

223
15:53.280 --> 15:54.280
What's stressing you out?

224
15:54.280 --> 15:55.760
I need to find a good piece of land

225
15:55.760 --> 15:56.360
at a good price.

226
15:56.400 --> 15:57.280
Any ideas where?

227
15:57.280 --> 15:59.040
How about Rayong? It's a major economic hub.

228
15:59.080 --> 16:01.440
Or Chiang Rai? It connects to both Laos and China.

229
16:01.480 --> 16:03.760
You're right. Thanks a lot, man.

230
16:07.040 --> 16:09.280
Stop thinking like that. It's just stupid.

231
16:11.040 --> 16:13.040
So you'll have the strength to keep pushing on.

232
16:20.200 --> 16:21.960
Hello? I'll send it right away.

233
16:22.000 --> 16:22.840
Sure.

234
16:24.640 --> 16:26.520
Yok, keep up, or you'll fall behind.

235
16:26.760 --> 16:27.800
Up here, right?

236
16:27.840 --> 16:29.240
Yes, put it down here instead.

237
16:29.280 --> 16:30.360
Yok, take notes.

238
16:30.800 --> 16:31.720
And over there...

239
16:32.560 --> 16:33.840
I'll go with this plan.

240
16:33.840 --> 16:35.360
Let's work together to make this project...

241
16:37.200 --> 16:38.600
Dinner is on me.

242
16:39.160 --> 16:41.760
You know the rule, no one's going home sober.

243
16:42.800 --> 16:43.920
You bet.

244
16:49.880 --> 16:50.920
Eat up.

245
16:50.960 --> 16:52.280
You've gotten so thin from working so hard.

246
16:52.760 --> 16:53.840
Take this, P'Phet.

247
16:54.800 --> 16:55.760
Aren't you eating?

248
16:55.960 --> 16:56.840
I'm fine.

249
16:58.640 --> 17:00.440
To be honest, I'm really glad

250
17:00.480 --> 17:01.400
I got to meet you today, Mr. Phet.

251
17:02.040 --> 17:04.440
Me, too. My brother mentions you quite often.

252
17:14.560 --> 17:15.359
Yes, Mr. Ing?

253
17:15.400 --> 17:16.400
Secretary Piang,

254
17:16.440 --> 17:17.480
have Yok come see me immediately.

255
17:21.640 --> 17:22.720
Understood.

256
17:28.359 --> 17:29.440
Go. Don't waste time,

257
17:29.480 --> 17:30.840
or he'll blow a fuse again.

258
17:33.880 --> 17:35.720
He doesn't want me anymore, I see.

259
17:38.400 --> 17:40.320
Mr. Ing, it's payday.

260
17:40.360 --> 17:41.640
I've already paid for the clothes.

261
17:42.040 --> 17:42.960
Forget about that.

262
17:43.480 --> 17:44.600
You're coming with me to Damnoen Saduak.

263
17:45.640 --> 17:46.480
What are we going there for?

264
17:47.880 --> 17:48.960
I'll tell you on the way.

265
17:54.080 --> 17:56.440
The proposals submitted to the government official

266
17:56.520 --> 17:57.680
suddenly ran into problems.

267
17:57.920 --> 17:58.800
All the documents

268
17:58.800 --> 18:00.040
have been sent back for revisions.

269
18:00.840 --> 18:02.880
The budget, the team,

270
18:02.920 --> 18:04.200
or the entire plan...

271
18:04.200 --> 18:05.600
We're waiting on a single document.

272
18:06.160 --> 18:07.440
I can't afford to mess this up.

273
18:07.680 --> 18:09.760
Getting a minister and investors together

274
18:09.800 --> 18:10.440
is no easy feat.

275
18:10.440 --> 18:11.800
We need to make this deal happen.

276
18:19.320 --> 18:20.800
Uncle Jeng, please turn the AC up.

277
18:20.800 --> 18:21.720
I'm freezing here.

278
18:22.080 --> 18:22.800
Understood.

279
18:24.840 --> 18:25.800
Do you have a cold?

280
18:26.280 --> 18:27.600
Should we stop and get some medicine?

281
18:28.320 --> 18:29.200
To nip it in the bud, you know.

282
18:29.200 --> 18:30.160
No need.

283
18:30.680 --> 18:32.760
It's nothing serious. I'll be fine after a quick nap.

284
18:33.200 --> 18:35.200
By the way, is that data ready?

285
18:35.240 --> 18:36.400
Let me have a look.

286
18:45.480 --> 18:46.760
I'm screwed.

287
18:46.920 --> 18:48.600
Yok, can you hold your liquor?

288
18:50.000 --> 18:50.840
Why do you ask?

289
18:51.960 --> 18:53.480
It's these investors.

290
18:53.720 --> 18:55.080
They drink like fish

291
18:55.400 --> 18:56.840
as if there's no tomorrow.

292
18:56.880 --> 18:58.240
They won't let us leave until we're wasted.

293
18:58.560 --> 19:01.200
Aren't you a heavy drinker yourself?

294
19:02.120 --> 19:03.440
Look at me now.

295
19:03.880 --> 19:05.600
After two glasses, I'll be down for the count.

296
19:06.920 --> 19:08.720
Anyway, book a hotel for me today.

297
19:09.480 --> 19:10.200
Sure.

298
19:10.240 --> 19:11.360
Make sure it's near the place.

299
19:11.640 --> 19:13.160
Hopefully, I'll be able to crawl back.

300
19:14.080 --> 19:15.480
Today is extremely important.

301
19:16.520 --> 19:18.520
Whether you drink or not,

302
19:18.680 --> 19:20.240
you have to keep me in check.

303
19:21.000 --> 19:22.640
We need to close this deal at any cost.

304
19:22.840 --> 19:24.200
If we can do that,

305
19:24.640 --> 19:25.320
we'll have the chance

306
19:25.320 --> 19:26.440
to move on to the Pattaya project.

307
19:26.480 --> 19:27.680
And if we pull it off,

308
19:27.680 --> 19:29.200
you'll have something to show off to your brother.

309
19:30.800 --> 19:32.560
This is just how business is.

310
19:36.440 --> 19:38.840
Having a successful father has its perks,

311
19:40.560 --> 19:42.080
but once you actually start working,

312
19:43.560 --> 19:45.320
people act all nice to your face,

313
19:46.320 --> 19:47.840
but behind your back? Jeez...

314
19:48.880 --> 19:49.960
It's a different story.

315
19:49.960 --> 19:51.440
They just go through the motions.

316
19:52.200 --> 19:53.440
I went through the same thing

317
19:53.440 --> 19:55.040
when I started out in my 20s.

318
19:56.360 --> 19:58.120
I thought people would respect me.

319
19:58.320 --> 19:59.520
Not a single one did.

320
20:00.400 --> 20:02.360
I faced all kinds of problems.

321
20:02.800 --> 20:03.640
Damn it.

322
20:05.200 --> 20:06.640
It's always just me.

323
20:11.680 --> 20:13.080
It's cold as hell.

324
20:20.400 --> 20:21.760
Get some sleep.

325
20:23.080 --> 20:24.320
I'll wake you up when we get there.

326
20:25.640 --> 20:27.080
I never would have guessed...

327
20:28.120 --> 20:29.600
that you're so good at taking care of people.

328
20:36.440 --> 20:37.800
Wake me up when we arrive.

329
20:45.320 --> 20:46.400
It's such an honor, Minister.

330
20:46.440 --> 20:47.840
-Please enjoy yourselves. -We will.

331
20:48.200 --> 20:50.800
Here's to destiny.

332
20:51.080 --> 20:53.080
Thank you, Minister Tawan

333
20:53.120 --> 20:54.840
and Mr. Ing,

334
20:54.840 --> 20:56.440
for honoring us with your presence today.

335
20:56.880 --> 20:58.680
-Cheers. -Cheers.

336
21:03.040 --> 21:05.000
This second glass is to sincerity.

337
21:06.280 --> 21:07.920
Whether our partnership succeeds...

338
21:07.960 --> 21:10.320
depends on how sincere we are with each other.

339
21:10.920 --> 21:12.160
Don't you agree, Mr. Ing?

340
21:16.960 --> 21:17.920
Have some more.

341
21:20.760 --> 21:22.000
Excellent.

342
21:22.600 --> 21:23.600
The third glass...

343
21:25.960 --> 21:27.560
I can't get out of this one, can I?

344
21:28.240 --> 21:30.160
Let this glass be...

345
21:30.200 --> 21:32.040
a testament to my sincerity to everyone.

346
21:35.600 --> 21:37.520
-Come on. -Let's go, bottoms up.

347
21:39.480 --> 21:41.920
If you want to do business with me, you need to be bold.

348
21:43.040 --> 21:45.520
Finish this, and I'll sign the contract right away.

349
21:52.400 --> 21:55.480
-Drink up. Drink up. -Drink up. Drink up.

350
21:55.600 --> 21:58.680
-Drink up. Drink up. -Drink up. Drink up.

351
21:58.760 --> 22:01.960
-Drink up. Drink up. -Drink up. Drink up.

352
22:04.440 --> 22:05.520
Please.

353
22:06.400 --> 22:07.400
Bottoms up.

354
22:07.400 --> 22:08.440
Empty it all.

355
22:11.840 --> 22:13.320
-Go for it. -Do it.

356
22:13.800 --> 22:15.560
-Drink. -Drink up.

357
22:16.440 --> 22:17.600
-Whoa. -Whoa.

358
22:19.240 --> 22:20.400
Mr. Jomthup,

359
22:20.760 --> 22:22.520
I'd like to take this drink on behalf of Mr. Ing.

360
22:22.920 --> 22:23.640
Yok...

361
22:24.760 --> 22:26.840
You might not understand how we do things here.

362
22:31.560 --> 22:32.440
Exactly.

363
22:32.920 --> 22:34.080
My father was just talking

364
22:34.080 --> 22:35.880
about you the other day, Mr. Jomthup.

365
22:36.320 --> 22:38.280
He enjoyed talking with you about the northern project.

366
22:41.520 --> 22:42.600
Mr. Ravit,

367
22:42.600 --> 22:44.920
my brother speaks very highly of your vision.

368
22:49.560 --> 22:50.800
Well then, let's go.

369
22:50.840 --> 22:51.840
Drink up.

370
22:51.880 --> 22:53.120
So, I'd like to raise this glass

371
22:53.120 --> 22:55.400
as a toast to my respect for all of you.

372
22:56.480 --> 22:57.360
It's our pleasure.

373
22:57.680 --> 22:58.760
-Bottoms up. -Drink.

374
22:58.760 --> 22:59.520
Drink.

375
23:00.520 --> 23:01.560
Not bad at all.

376
23:04.280 --> 23:05.520
Have another round.

377
23:05.800 --> 23:07.560
-Keep them coming. -Another one.

378
23:07.600 --> 23:10.240
There's still some left. Keep it going.

379
23:10.280 --> 23:11.040
Don't stop.

380
23:24.680 --> 23:25.800
P'Ing, stay still.

381
23:56.800 --> 23:57.600
Wait.

382
24:00.520 --> 24:01.600
Normally...

383
24:03.520 --> 24:05.200
aren't you someone

384
24:05.240 --> 24:07.600
who can separate work from personal life?

385
24:08.560 --> 24:11.000
Taking care of my boss is part of my job.

386
24:13.200 --> 24:15.760
Your boss never taught you anything like this.

387
24:17.840 --> 24:19.120
I'm leaving, then.

388
24:21.000 --> 24:21.800
Hold on.

389
24:23.280 --> 24:24.160
Come here.

390
24:25.080 --> 24:25.920
Come over here.

391
24:32.520 --> 24:33.240
Look...

392
24:34.600 --> 24:35.520
Just a second.

393
24:46.320 --> 24:47.280
I feel better now.

394
24:49.640 --> 24:50.720
Much better.

395
24:52.240 --> 24:53.680
You're quite good at taking care of people.

396
24:54.520 --> 24:57.000
Thanks a lot. I feel a lot better now.

397
24:58.640 --> 25:01.240
Go wash your shirt. It's filthy.

398
25:18.000 --> 25:18.800
Get out of the car.

399
25:29.600 --> 25:31.160
We drove all this way...

400
25:31.160 --> 25:32.600
just to look at a wasteland?

401
25:33.400 --> 25:35.000
This isn't just any ordinary wasteland.

402
25:35.200 --> 25:38.080
It's the fruit of our success from yesterday.

403
25:41.160 --> 25:42.160
Come to think of it...

404
25:43.800 --> 25:45.760
you can really hold your liquor, can't you?

405
25:46.920 --> 25:48.480
I never would've pegged you for that type.

406
25:49.400 --> 25:51.320
To be honest, if I weren't sick,

407
25:51.840 --> 25:54.080
I would've outdrunk those old geezers.

408
25:56.360 --> 25:57.800
So, are you recovered now?

409
25:58.320 --> 25:59.080
Of course.

410
26:00.080 --> 26:01.120
I'm fit as a fiddle.

411
26:01.160 --> 26:02.120
If you don't believe me...

412
26:03.560 --> 26:04.440
want to find out?

413
26:06.000 --> 26:07.520
You're never going to stop, are you?

414
26:08.240 --> 26:10.600
Jeez, why so serious?

415
26:11.680 --> 26:12.280
Alright.

416
26:13.240 --> 26:13.880
We're here.

417
26:18.400 --> 26:19.800
From now on, this area...

418
26:20.920 --> 26:23.160
will be where your first building stands.

419
26:25.360 --> 26:26.280
My first building?

420
26:27.200 --> 26:27.960
Yes.

421
26:31.280 --> 26:32.560
This will be...

422
26:33.080 --> 26:35.320
the first building you'll oversee for this project.

423
26:38.240 --> 26:39.200
What's with the confused look?

424
26:40.200 --> 26:41.120
No need to get sentimental.

425
26:41.720 --> 26:43.120
You've earned it, Yok.

426
26:48.920 --> 26:50.120
Aren't you going to set foot

427
26:50.160 --> 26:51.880
on the site you'll be managing?

428
27:17.560 --> 27:18.560
From now on,

429
27:20.320 --> 27:22.240
this area is your responsibility.

430
27:33.480 --> 27:35.320
Alright, we should get moving.

431
27:36.200 --> 27:38.400
There's someone important I want to introduce.

432
27:42.680 --> 27:43.880
Why are you just standing there?

433
27:44.400 --> 27:45.040
Hurry up.

434
28:02.000 --> 28:03.240
Where are we?

435
28:41.080 --> 28:41.920
You little rascal.

436
28:44.840 --> 28:46.960
Finally decided to visit your grandpa, huh?

437
28:47.920 --> 28:50.120
Grandpa, that was a pretty hard pat on the back.

438
28:50.320 --> 28:52.480
Judging by that strength, you'll probably...

439
28:53.000 --> 28:54.640
live to be at least a hundred and twenty.

440
28:55.400 --> 28:57.040
Why would I want to live that long?

441
28:57.600 --> 28:58.120
Tell me if you're lonely.

442
28:58.160 --> 28:58.920
I'll find you a wife.

443
29:00.240 --> 29:00.880
Are you serious?

444
29:01.200 --> 29:02.400
Come on, let's head inside.

445
29:04.040 --> 29:04.720
Oh?

446
29:05.080 --> 29:06.400
Whose kid is this?

447
29:06.680 --> 29:09.320
This is Minister Pongpaisan's son.

448
29:09.440 --> 29:10.360
He's interning with me,

449
29:10.400 --> 29:12.400
so I brought him along to meet you.

450
29:12.440 --> 29:14.840
I see, so it's Pong's grandson.

451
29:16.080 --> 29:17.560
You certainly have a keen eye for people.

452
29:18.720 --> 29:20.880
Hello, Grandpa. I'm Yok.

453
29:20.960 --> 29:23.960
My, look how much you've grown.

454
29:24.400 --> 29:25.680
When you were just a little thing,

455
29:25.880 --> 29:27.480
I used to carry you around.

456
29:27.600 --> 29:28.960
Not that you'd remember.

457
29:29.200 --> 29:31.600
Your grandfather was a stubborn man.

458
29:31.720 --> 29:33.800
He was dead set on giving you a girl's name.

459
29:34.440 --> 29:37.040
He said Yok, or jade, is as precious as diamonds.

460
29:37.320 --> 29:40.360
Everyone tried to stop him, of course,

461
29:41.000 --> 29:42.720
but no one could change his mind.

462
29:44.720 --> 29:46.200
It's a good thing they couldn't.

463
29:47.400 --> 29:49.320
I think this piece of jade is...

464
29:50.200 --> 29:51.400
quite precious indeed.

465
29:53.640 --> 29:55.320
Why are we standing here baking in the sun?

466
29:55.320 --> 29:56.600
Let's go inside.

467
29:56.920 --> 29:58.520
-It's boiling out here. Follow me. -Alright.

468
30:11.800 --> 30:12.800
Know what tree this is?

469
30:14.200 --> 30:16.000
This is called a Pong-pong tree.

470
30:16.040 --> 30:17.480
Don't ever eat those fruits.

471
30:17.520 --> 30:18.800
They're lethal.

472
30:19.080 --> 30:20.360
And this one...

473
30:22.840 --> 30:24.360
When I was a kid, Grandpa tricked me.

474
30:24.400 --> 30:26.120
He told me it was a banana tree.

475
30:26.160 --> 30:27.720
I waited for it to bear fruit,

476
30:27.760 --> 30:29.040
but in the end, it didn't.

477
30:30.800 --> 30:31.840
This one...

478
30:32.680 --> 30:33.880
is a Ti plant.

479
30:34.800 --> 30:35.640
Pretty, isn't it?

480
30:37.920 --> 30:39.400
Not as pretty as me, I guess.

481
30:44.720 --> 30:45.720
Look at this.

482
30:46.320 --> 30:47.840
I got some pond snails yesterday.

483
30:48.080 --> 30:49.560
I'm going to make a red curry for you.

484
30:50.880 --> 30:53.440
You two, go catch some fish.

485
30:53.560 --> 30:56.000
I want two big...

486
30:56.040 --> 30:56.760
nice ones.

487
30:56.800 --> 30:58.720
Putting us to work again?

488
30:58.960 --> 31:00.560
Yong has the fishing rods ready for you.

489
31:00.560 --> 31:01.640
Same old rule.

490
31:02.000 --> 31:04.880
If the fish don't weigh at least two kilograms,

491
31:04.920 --> 31:07.680
you have to do the dishes tonight.

492
31:07.720 --> 31:08.520
Okay.

493
31:09.440 --> 31:10.400
Just like always, right?

494
31:10.760 --> 31:11.560
Did you hear that?

495
31:11.840 --> 31:13.280
If you don't want your hands getting all pruney...

496
31:13.920 --> 31:14.920
show me what you've got.

497
31:17.840 --> 31:19.240
Grandpa, he's just putting on an act.

498
31:19.280 --> 31:20.640
He usually knows how to smile.

499
31:23.680 --> 31:24.440
He just smiles.

500
31:24.480 --> 31:25.400
You got it, Grandpa.

501
31:26.400 --> 31:27.320
Oh, so you can talk.

502
31:39.440 --> 31:41.120
You brought me all this way just to fish?

503
31:42.920 --> 31:43.600
Yok,

504
31:44.040 --> 31:44.960
let me ask you something.

505
31:46.200 --> 31:47.440
How were you raised?

506
31:48.560 --> 31:49.520
Why do you have to

507
31:49.560 --> 31:51.480
question everything before doing anything?

508
31:52.320 --> 31:54.080
We're humans. Just do whatever you want.

509
31:54.680 --> 31:56.760
Want to swim? Swim. Want to fish? Fish.

510
31:56.800 --> 31:57.680
Eat whatever you want.

511
31:58.200 --> 31:59.560
Why overthink everything?

512
32:06.800 --> 32:07.600
Come on.

513
32:10.040 --> 32:11.200
Why are you just standing there?

514
32:11.240 --> 32:12.480
Hurry and bring me some water.

515
32:14.640 --> 32:15.480
Hurry up.

516
32:24.160 --> 32:25.240
Why aren't you coming?

517
32:25.280 --> 32:26.720
Scared of me?

518
32:36.920 --> 32:39.560
Aw, you're scaring me now.

519
32:43.920 --> 32:44.560
What?

520
32:52.680 --> 32:53.800
How do you like that?

521
32:54.320 --> 32:55.320
Having fun, huh?

522
32:57.920 --> 32:58.640
P'Ing...

523
32:58.960 --> 32:59.680
P'Ing.

524
33:09.040 --> 33:11.280
P'Ing, aren't we fishing anymore?

525
33:11.320 --> 33:13.200
Come on, forget about the fish.

526
33:13.240 --> 33:15.000
Let's just swim for now.

527
33:27.720 --> 33:28.600
You little rascal.

528
33:29.200 --> 33:31.800
I told you to fish, but all you did was swim.

529
33:33.160 --> 33:34.720
You've been like this since you were a kid.

530
33:35.520 --> 33:36.680
You haven't changed either, Grandpa.

531
33:37.080 --> 33:39.040
Still nagging me after all these years.

532
33:39.080 --> 33:40.400
Thailand is just so hot, you know?

533
33:40.440 --> 33:41.680
Didn't I catch the fish

534
33:41.680 --> 33:43.320
you wanted, anyway?

535
33:43.360 --> 33:45.360
We got about three or four kilos, right?

536
33:46.320 --> 33:46.880
Yes.

537
33:48.200 --> 33:49.520
You're quite something, aren't you?

538
33:53.440 --> 33:54.840
Hey, where are you going?

539
33:55.800 --> 33:56.680
I've got the good stuff.

540
34:00.400 --> 34:01.320
He means the liquor.

541
34:01.480 --> 34:02.440
Have some.

542
34:06.200 --> 34:07.440
Yong, bring the glasses over here.

543
34:10.440 --> 34:13.960
This is Karanda fruit.

544
34:14.840 --> 34:18.560
I grew it and pickled it with my own two hands.

545
34:19.480 --> 34:20.040
Now...

546
34:20.080 --> 34:20.880
Give me the glasses.

547
34:21.400 --> 34:22.239
Who do you think I take after?

548
34:22.520 --> 34:23.320
Here.

549
34:28.400 --> 34:31.400
-Make sure you look after your health, too. -Alright.

550
34:34.199 --> 34:35.280
Here.

551
34:35.880 --> 34:36.639
Three shots.

552
34:38.920 --> 34:41.360
Wait, Grandpa. I'll drink with you.

553
34:41.400 --> 34:42.520
Yok doesn't drink.

554
34:50.480 --> 34:52.040
That's a very unique flavor.

555
34:53.760 --> 34:55.800
I thought you said he didn't drink.

556
34:57.720 --> 34:59.040
Look who's got egg on his face.

557
34:59.400 --> 35:01.280
Look at you, you little puppy...

558
35:02.320 --> 35:04.080
Traveling all this way,

559
35:05.240 --> 35:06.200
don't tell me...

560
35:06.240 --> 35:08.120
that you only came here just to visit me.

561
35:09.520 --> 35:11.080
What kind of trouble are you cooking up this time?

562
35:12.000 --> 35:14.560
Come on, you're accusing me already?

563
35:14.600 --> 35:16.200
Are you really my grandpa or what?

564
35:16.320 --> 35:18.000
Of course I am.

565
35:18.040 --> 35:20.200
Why else would I bother worrying about you?

566
35:21.120 --> 35:25.080
So, what are you really doing here?

567
35:29.520 --> 35:30.720
Okay, you win.

568
35:30.760 --> 35:33.440
It's just about the hotel project.

569
35:34.560 --> 35:35.680
The connections hit a snag,

570
35:35.680 --> 35:36.560
so things are getting delayed.

571
35:36.600 --> 35:38.320
I've already sunk all my money into it.

572
35:38.360 --> 35:38.920
Eventually,

573
35:38.920 --> 35:40.560
I'll have to find a new way forward.

574
35:41.880 --> 35:43.080
You don't need to worry at all.

575
35:44.320 --> 35:46.880
Looking for a way out is one thing,

576
35:47.320 --> 35:48.400
but don't break the rules.

577
35:48.760 --> 35:49.360
I know.

578
35:49.400 --> 35:51.840
Don't think having a reputation

579
35:51.880 --> 35:52.760
means you'll get a free pass.

580
35:53.120 --> 35:54.320
Focus on your work

581
35:54.640 --> 35:56.680
and keep yourself on the right track.

582
35:56.880 --> 35:57.680
Do you hear me?

583
35:58.600 --> 36:00.360
Understood.

584
36:00.400 --> 36:01.560
I hear you.

585
36:02.680 --> 36:04.720
Ing here is quite hot-tempered.

586
36:05.520 --> 36:07.520
Don't let him lead you astray.

587
36:07.880 --> 36:09.280
What, Grandpa?

588
36:09.520 --> 36:12.960
How could someone like me lead him astray?

589
36:14.240 --> 36:16.040
P'Ing has been taking very good care of me.

590
36:17.000 --> 36:17.800
Well said.

591
36:20.160 --> 36:21.880
Then let's have dinner.

592
36:21.880 --> 36:22.840
Come on.

593
36:24.320 --> 36:26.240
Yok, keep telling me more

594
36:26.280 --> 36:27.680
about your grandfather.

595
36:28.320 --> 36:29.080
Of course.

596
36:30.760 --> 36:32.360
Have some curry with pond snails.

597
36:32.360 --> 36:33.600
I made it myself.

598
36:41.120 --> 36:41.920
Honestly,

599
36:42.920 --> 36:44.760
I feel for you.

600
36:44.800 --> 36:45.360
Here we go again.

601
36:45.400 --> 36:47.000
When you were a kid,

602
36:47.000 --> 36:48.720
what you went through...

603
36:50.240 --> 36:52.920
was more than anyone could take.

604
36:53.120 --> 36:54.880
If your mother were still around...

605
36:54.920 --> 36:56.200
That's enough, Grandpa.

606
36:56.680 --> 36:57.760
That was a long time ago,

607
36:57.800 --> 36:59.960
and it's all in the past now.

608
37:00.120 --> 37:00.880
You don't have to worry.

609
37:00.880 --> 37:03.560
I'm not gonna jump off a building over this.

610
37:04.000 --> 37:07.000
That's just how old people are. We talk and talk.

611
37:08.720 --> 37:09.840
Anyway, you two...

612
37:10.920 --> 37:12.440
must be exhausted by now.

613
37:13.480 --> 37:14.360
I'm getting sleepy.

614
37:14.360 --> 37:15.200
Not at all.

615
37:15.760 --> 37:17.440
-What? -I've enjoyed talking with you, Grandpa.

616
37:19.240 --> 37:21.560
This one is quite the smooth talker.

617
37:23.400 --> 37:27.080
If only Ing were half as smooth-talking as you are,

618
37:27.440 --> 37:29.720
I'd be much more at ease.

619
37:30.720 --> 37:31.640
Not at all.

620
37:31.640 --> 37:33.320
I've enjoyed talking with you, Grandpa.

621
37:34.720 --> 37:35.640
You really are something...

622
37:36.720 --> 37:38.640
Hey, Yong.

623
37:38.680 --> 37:39.760
That's enough, Grandpa.

624
37:39.760 --> 37:40.920
-Go... -Grandpa.

625
37:40.960 --> 37:42.960
I'll have him get the guest room ready for Yok.

626
37:43.200 --> 37:45.400
Yok and I can just share my room.

627
37:45.720 --> 37:47.520
Right? We don't mind a bit of a squeeze.

628
37:50.800 --> 37:51.880
Right, the silent treatment.

629
37:52.440 --> 37:53.200
I'll take that as a yes.

630
37:55.000 --> 37:56.000
Thanks for having me.

631
37:57.840 --> 37:59.560
Take good care of Yok, alright?

632
38:03.720 --> 38:04.320
I will.

633
38:11.320 --> 38:12.120
Sorry about this.

634
38:12.840 --> 38:16.560
My grandpa is all about that low-carbon lifestyle,

635
38:17.120 --> 38:20.000
so there's no AC. Just this old-school fan.

636
38:20.640 --> 38:22.160
You can handle it, right?

637
38:23.280 --> 38:24.840
It's fine. It's not that hot anyway.

638
38:40.600 --> 38:41.880
I'm going to hit the shower.

639
38:43.520 --> 38:44.320
Don't you dare peek.

640
39:15.320 --> 39:16.440
It's your turn now.

641
39:22.920 --> 39:23.520
Yok...

642
39:26.400 --> 39:27.000
Yok,

643
39:27.360 --> 39:28.000
wake up.

644
39:31.440 --> 39:32.720
Go take a shower.

645
39:33.960 --> 39:35.080
No...

646
39:35.680 --> 39:36.720
You have to.

647
39:37.080 --> 39:38.960
How can you go to bed without showering first?

648
39:39.360 --> 39:40.600
Go shower.

649
39:41.520 --> 39:43.760
Go take a shower.

650
39:47.680 --> 39:48.480
Go.

651
39:52.640 --> 39:54.360
Your towel is over here.

652
40:03.040 --> 40:04.320
He ruined everything.

653
40:12.880 --> 40:13.720
Oh...

654
40:15.120 --> 40:18.560
I spilled some water all over the blanket.

655
40:19.640 --> 40:20.800
We'll have to share this one.

656
40:23.160 --> 40:24.400
Hurry up and turn off the lights.

657
40:25.440 --> 40:26.520
Get to bed.

658
40:56.280 --> 40:56.880
Hey.

659
40:59.240 --> 41:01.080
Aren't you hot in long sleeves?

660
41:02.520 --> 41:03.400
I'm not.

661
41:06.720 --> 41:08.520
You'll be too hot to sleep in a bit. Come here.

662
41:09.040 --> 41:10.560
-Let me help you take them off. -I'm fine.

663
41:25.840 --> 41:28.320
What? I was just trying to tuck you in.

664
41:33.480 --> 41:34.520
Suit yourself.

665
41:35.120 --> 41:36.240
If you don't want the blanket, fine.

666
41:37.600 --> 41:39.440
Don't come crying to me if you get sick.

667
41:40.920 --> 41:41.840
Earlier today,

668
41:41.880 --> 41:43.200
you didn't seem to care if I got sick.

669
41:44.440 --> 41:46.720
Why are you holding such a grudge?

670
42:04.520 --> 42:06.840
Sorry, I'm a side sleeper.

671
42:22.400 --> 42:24.440
-What are you doing? -I'm just trying to cover you up.

672
42:25.800 --> 42:26.920
Wait, where are you going?

673
42:26.920 --> 42:28.600
I'm just trying to tuck you in.

674
42:28.600 --> 42:29.720
It's nothing.

675
42:29.720 --> 42:31.600
Come here. I told you to cover up.

676
42:37.560 --> 42:38.440
That hurts.

677
42:52.000 --> 42:53.200
Wait, where are you going?

678
42:57.960 --> 42:59.160
Come visit again when you're free.

679
42:59.200 --> 43:00.280
Grandpa, I'm not leaving soon.

680
43:00.320 --> 43:01.200
Who was talking to you?

681
43:01.360 --> 43:01.960
Grandpa...

682
43:02.600 --> 43:03.720
Just who is your actual grandson here?

683
43:04.120 --> 43:04.680
Hey.

684
43:05.280 --> 43:06.200
Want to try dating each other?

685
43:07.160 --> 43:08.600
Whether I like women or not,

686
43:08.640 --> 43:10.000
there's no way we could be together.

687
43:12.560 --> 43:14.280
I've endured this for long enough.
